00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:03.669 align:start position:0%
this is the seventh round of  negotiations between iran and  signatories of the 2015 nuclear deal as  well as the united states  and one of the main sticking points for  the europeans had been iran's compliance  with the international atomic energy  agency until now  last night we reached a good agreement  with the iaea that could address some of  the alleged concerns about iran's  peaceful nuclear program and lead to  continued mutual cooperation with the  iaea  two series of texts are being discussed  in vienna the first is the result of six  rounds of talks at the same time other  parties have agreed to have iran's newly  proposed texts on the table so as to  achieve a single concise text from  discussions and combination of all of  these  iran says the iea will not be able to  allow to have cameras at one of its  sensitive sites  the director general of the un nuclear  watchdog has had some serious concerns  about the lack of access to what was  taking place at a workshop just outside  tehran where centrifuges are being made  but in june one of the cameras was  attacked and damaged  iranian officials accused israel of  sabotage  then iranian officials took all four  iaea cameras offline and refused to  allow inspectors to replace them now  with this technical agreement with the  iaea there is hope that the talks here  in vienna will get the push they need to  move forward in a practical sense it  means that the iaea again  will be able to monitor the production  of centrifuge components  this is what the garage facility does  and the reason for doing this is for the  iaea to have a better handle  on whether any centrifuge components  might be taken away from karaj  to be assembled into centrifuges at some  secret site  the remaining signatories of the nuclear  deal have been meeting since april to  try and get the u.s and iran to return  to the agreement which was aimed at  limiting iran's nuclear program in  exchange for economic benefits and  sanctions relief while the u.s is not  directly talking to iranian officials  here in vienna there seems to be renewed  optimism about the seventh round of  talks and now that the main issue  between iran and the iaea seems to be  resolved it will be up to the americans  to put forth what they're willing to do  to convince iran to return to full  compliance  dorsojabari al jazeera vienna
 

